wsl
  ✓ WSL 2 (Ubuntu), Windows interop on
  ! systemd is not running in this distro, so devlanes daemon install cannot start the daemon with it
    fix: set systemd=true under [boot] in /etc/wsl.conf, then run wsl.exe --shutdown from Windows and reopen the distro
  ✓ NAT networking: Windows reaches the proxy through WSL's localhost forwarding
  ! ports below 1024 need root in this distro, so the proxy cannot bind 80 and 443 and uses its fallback ports (8080 for HTTP, 8443 for HTTPS)
    fix: sudo sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start=80, and keep it with echo net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start=80 | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/50-devlanes.conf; then devlanes daemon restart
  ✓ WSL rewrites /etc/hosts when the distro starts (generateHosts); the daemon writes its names again when it starts, and Windows programs never read this file
  ! browsers on Windows do not trust the CA: tls.trust leaves out windows
    fix: add windows to tls.trust in ~/.devlanes/config.yaml, then devlanes certs trust
  ! acme@2 is on the Windows drive C:\ (/mnt/c/src/acme-2): file access is slow and file watching misses edits made from Windows
    fix: move the repository to the Linux filesystem, for example ~/src
proxy
  ! http on fallback port 8080: port 80 needs root
    fix: free the standard port or set proxy ports in ~/.devlanes/config.yaml
  ! https on fallback port 8443: port 443 needs root
    fix: free the standard port or set proxy ports in ~/.devlanes/config.yaml
